{
    "background_story": "Angel was a mysterious and introverted artist, known for her captivating portraits that seemed to reveal the deepest secrets of her subjects. She had a habit of observing people with sidelong glances, as if trying to catch a glimpse of their true selves. Her friends and family often joked that she could see right through them with her piercing gaze. One day, while working on a new piece, Angel caught a sidelong glance of a stranger on the street. She was struck by the hint of sadness in his eyes and felt an overwhelming urge to capture his story on canvas. The resulting portrait, titled 'The Unseen', became her most famous work, showcasing her unique ability to convey the complexities of the human experience through a single, sidelong glance.",
